  "body": "**PR 1 of 3.** Data only — no behaviour change. The next PR consumes this and changes what goes on the wire; keeping them apart means that one can be reviewed as the behaviour change it actually is.\n\n## The problem\n\nReasoning is translated **per provider**, with no per-**model** knowledge. `ReasoningEncoder.encode(body, policy)` receives no model information at all and fires unconditionally.\n\nThat is how a numeric budget reached a model that only accepts an effort enum (see v5.31.1, Fireworks), and how `xhigh` reaches a model whose vocabulary stops at `high`.\n\n## The find\n\nmodels.dev publishes exactly the missing data — and **this project already fetches and disk-caches that index** for cost, context limit and vision, then discards every reasoning field.\n\n```json\n\"reasoning\": true,\n\"reasoning_options\": [{\"type\":\"toggle\"},\n                      {\"type\":\"effort\",\"values\":[\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]},\n                      {\"type\":\"budget_tokens\"}]\n```\n\nMeasured against the live 4 MB index:\n\n```\n192 providers, 6838 models, 4718 reasoning-capable\nreasoning_options: effort 2515 | toggle 1081 | budget_tokens 587\neffort values: none, minimal, low, medium, high, xhigh, max\n```\n\nThe effort vocabulary is **identical** to this project's `ReasoningEffort` enum, and the three option types map **one-to-one** onto the encoder families already in the code (`NamedEffortReasoning` / `ThinkingObjectReasoning` / the budget path).\n\nCoverage for this project's 56 providers: **42 resolve** (with an alias map), covering 2,569 models of which 1,276 carry `reasoning_options`. The 14 with no entry — `agnes`, `commandcode`, `featherless`, `llamacpp`, `mistral_codestral`, `nararoute`, `nous_portal`, `ollama`, `opencode_go`, `qwencloud`, `qwencloud_coding`, `sambanova`, `tokenrouter`, `wafer` — resolve to unknown, never an error.\n\n## What this adds\n\n- **`ModelReasoningCapability`** beside `ProviderModelInfo`. Three independent control-style booleans rather than one enum, because a model can advertise several at once and callers ask about each separately. Every field's `None` means **unknown**, deliberately distinct from a known `False` — the consumer must only change behaviour for capabilities it can confirm.\n- **Parsing** of `reasoning`/`reasoning_options`, tolerating malformed entries and dropping value strings that are not `ReasoningEffort` members (the stray `\"default\"`) rather than raising.\n- **A lookup**, layered `provider-reported → models.dev → None`.\n\n## The trap this deliberately avoids\n\nThe lookup reads the **disk** cache, never the in-memory `ProviderModelCache`.\n\nThat cache is populated *only* by the admin `/admin/api/models/refresh` endpoint and is **empty on a fresh server**. A lookup gated on it would leave this entire feature silently never firing — the exact failure mode this project has hit four separate times. There is a test named for that specific trap, and it is mutation-verified.\n\n## Verification\n\n```\n39 tests pass (20 new)\nfull suite  4455 passed, 14 pre-existing baseline\nruff format / ruff check / ty check   clean repo-wide\n```\n\nMutation-tested, each confirmed failing by name:\n\n```\ndrop an alias from the map            -> 3 tests failed\nreturn a default record, not None,\n  for an absent model                 -> 4 tests failed (unknown/known-false collapse)\ngate lookup on empty in-memory cache  -> the named trap test failed\n```\n\n**Verified against the real 4 MB index, not only the fixture** — a parser that handles its own test data is not a parser that handles models.dev:\n\n```\nopen_router  anthropic/claude-opus-4.5   -> can_reason=True effort=True toggle=True budget=True\n                                             efforts=['high','low','medium']\ndeepseek     deepseek-chat               -> can_reason=False   (known-false, not unknown)\ngroq         openai/gpt-oss-120b         -> effort=True  efforts=['high','low','medium']\nfireworks    accounts/.../kimi-k2p6-fast -> toggle-only: effort=False budget=False\nwafer        anything                    -> UNKNOWN (None)\n\nalias entries: 18, resolving to a REAL provider: 18\nmemoised lookup: 21.1 microseconds/call over 2000 calls\n```\n\n## Proof of no behaviour change\n\n`git diff --stat` touches three files: the dataclass, the models.dev parser, and its tests. No encoder, no request builder, no routing file. The new functions are currently **unreferenced** — nothing calls them, so no code path's behaviour changed.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n**models.dev is hand-curated and externally maintained**, so we inherit its update lag; a brand-new model may be absent for a while. That degrades to unknown, which the next PR treats as \"behave exactly as today\", so the failure mode is *no improvement*, never a regression.\n\n**Model-id matching is string normalisation**, reusing the existing `_normalize_candidates`. A provider whose model ids diverge from models.dev's spelling will resolve to unknown rather than mismatch — verified for the 14 uncovered providers.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti\n",
